From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: menu rows grow with their content; Quick Options opens centred

Luma's compact context menus fixed every popup menu row at 32px. That
applied to every menu in the Shell, not only context menus: Tiling's
layout grid in Quick Options and Tiling Shell's own layout menu painted
over the actions beneath them, and device and network rows put their
icon below their name. Rows now have a 32px minimum and grow with what
they hold; Quick Options detail rows keep their own compact sizing.

Quick Options was anchored at its left edge to the centre of the clock
and status island and extended off to its right. It now opens centred
over the island, as the dock's menus do.

--- a/data/theme/gnome-shell-dark.css
+++ b/data/theme/gnome-shell-dark.css
@@ -3755,7 +3755,7 @@
 .background-menu .popup-menu-content { min-width: 204px; }
 .app-menu .popup-menu-content { min-width: 174px; padding: 5px; }
 .popup-menu-item {
-  height: 32px; min-height: 0;
+  min-height: 32px;
   padding: 0 8px; spacing: 10px;
   border: none; border-radius: 10px;
   color: #f2f4f6; background-color: transparent;
--- a/data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css
+++ b/data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css
@@ -3943,7 +3943,7 @@
